9
00:00:11,910 --> 00:00:13,935
So let's look at what American

10
00:00:13,955 --> 00:00:15,412
families actually have,

11
00:00:15,432 --> 00:00:17,173
using the Federal Reserve's

12
00:00:17,193 --> 00:00:18,539
newest numbers.

13
00:00:18,559 --> 00:00:19,305
By the end,

14
00:00:19,325 --> 00:00:20,892
you'll know exactly where

15
00:00:20,912 --> 00:00:21,548
you stand,

16
00:00:21,568 --> 00:00:23,026
and why you're probably

17
00:00:23,046 --> 00:00:25,177
not as behind as you feel.

18
00:00:25,197 --> 00:00:25,617
First,

19
00:00:25,637 --> 00:00:26,584
a trap.

20
00:00:26,604 --> 00:00:28,620
The Federal Reserve's 2025

21
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:30,792
Survey of Consumer Finances

22
00:00:30,812 --> 00:00:32,829
says the average American

23
00:00:32,849 --> 00:00:34,933
family is worth about one

24
00:00:34,953 --> 00:00:37,777
