and it feels harder lately,

84
00:02:10,017 --> 00:02:11,768
you're not imagining it.

85
00:02:11,788 --> 00:02:13,844
The median net worth for

86
00:02:13,864 --> 00:02:15,851
families under thirty-five

87
00:02:15,871 --> 00:02:18,342
actually fell about twenty-three

88
00:02:18,362 --> 00:02:20,349
percent between 2022 and

89
00:02:20,369 --> 00:02:21,164
2025.

90
00:02:21,184 --> 00:02:22,710
So if you're young and your

91
00:02:22,730 --> 00:02:23,741
number looks small,

92
00:02:23,761 --> 00:02:25,240
you're looking at the start

93
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:25,989
of the curve,

94
00:02:26,009 --> 00:02:27,092
not the end.

95
00:02:27,112 --> 00:02:27,385
Now,

96
00:02:27,405 --> 00:02:27,737
cash.

97
00:02:27,757 --> 00:02:29,556
How much does the typical

98
00:02:29,576 --> 00:02:31,199
family keep in checking

99
00:02:31,219 --> 00:02:32,421
and savings?

100
00:02:32,441 --> 00:02:34,074
The median is about eight

101
00:02:34,094 --> 00:02:36,233
thousand two hundred dollars.

102
00:02:36,253 --> 00:02:37,238
Eight thousand.

103
00:02:37,258 --> 00:02:37,888
That's it.

104
00:02:37,908 --> 00:02:39,189
Not fifty thousand.

105
00:02:39,209 --> 00:02:41,244
Not a year of expenses.

106
00:02:41,264 --> 00:02:42,750
So if you have even one

107
00:02:42,770 --> 00:02:44,155
month of expenses saved,

108
00:02:44,175 --> 00:02:45,561
you're doing better than

109
00:02:45,581 --> 00:02:47,316
