134
00:03:23,250 --> 00:03:24,522
account at all.

135
00:03:24,542 --> 00:03:25,671
That's a 401(k),

136
00:03:25,691 --> 00:03:26,317
an IRA,

137
00:03:26,337 --> 00:03:27,435
anything.

138
00:03:27,455 --> 00:03:28,816
Which means almost half

139
00:03:28,836 --> 00:03:30,345
have nothing set aside in

140
00:03:30,365 --> 00:03:30,991
one.

141
00:03:31,011 --> 00:03:32,916
Among families that do have

142
00:03:32,936 --> 00:03:33,208
one,

143
00:03:33,228 --> 00:03:35,133
the median balance is about

144
00:03:35,153 --> 00:03:36,825
one hundred six thousand

145
00:03:36,845 --> 00:03:37,750
dollars.

146
00:03:37,770 --> 00:03:39,278
If you have a retirement

147
00:03:39,298 --> 00:03:39,736
account,

148
00:03:39,756 --> 00:03:40,398
any amount,

149
00:03:40,418 --> 00:03:41,773
you're already ahead of

150
00:03:41,793 --> 00:03:43,599
nearly half the country.

151
00:03:43,619 --> 00:03:45,106
So why does it feel like

152
00:03:45,126 --> 00:03:46,964
everyone is ahead of you?

153
00:03:46,984 --> 00:03:47,727
Reason one:

154
00:03:47,747 --> 00:03:49,253
you're seeing highlight

155
00:03:49,273 --> 00:03:49,663
reels.

156
00:03:49,683 --> 00:03:51,365
People post the new car,

157
00:03:51,385 --> 00:03:52,997
not the car loan.

158
00:03:53,017 --> 00:03:53,778
Reason two:

159
00:03:53,798 --> 00:03:55,702
you're comparing to averages,

160
00:03:55,722 --> 00:03:57,806
and we just saw how averages

161
00:03:57,826 --> 00:03:58,506
lie.

162
00:03:58,526 --> 00:03:59,298
Reason three:

163
00:03:59,318 --> 00:04:00,776
you're comparing yourself

164
00:04:00,796 --> 00:04:02,413
